I don't think that you will lose anything but your life... :-).

You *do* know that if you take him on in melee, he has a chance of 
instantly beheading you?

There are of course ways to deal with him.  A pretty safe approach is 
using firearms.  Read a (blessed) scroll of earth while standing just 
outside the entrance.  Take your pick-axe out of the bag.  Sam will 
immediately stand in front of the entrance to block it.  Then send him 
bullets using your trusty assault rifle (or submachine gun, takes a 
little longer).  You will need to kill him twice, because he wears an 
amulet of life saving.  So reckon to spend something like 25 bullets on him.

The only problem I see with this approach is that he *might* have a wand 
of striking (has not happened to me yet) and destroy the boulder that 
separates him from you.  Either verify that he has not by zapping a wand 
of probing at him or else pulverize the boulder to your north before 
attacking him, so you can run, once he comes after you.  I believe, if 
you are invisible, he will not come out of his shop, but I am not sure.

After you are done with him, you'll have to get rid of his assistants. 
They are not particularly dangerous, but one of them (Izzy) is a 
rhaumbusun that can paralyze you, allowing the cockatrices to take care 
of you.  So you need a ring of free action or a blindfold (I *believe* 
being blind protects you from the rhaumbusun's gaze, but I am not sure - 
I am still far from being a slashem expert :-) ). Alternatively, zap a 
wand of create monster while still on friendly terms with Sam, until you 
get a dog, make him your pet by throwing some appropriate food and let 
him deal with the rhaumbusun (Sam won't object, and a large dog is 
capable of killing a rhaumbusun; if you yourself attack one of Sam's 
assistants, he *will* of course get angry).

Ah, and get your hands on Thiefbane, once you are done with Sam, but 
don't use it against the demon in his shop...
